tent":false,"epmc_pair":7,"lift":2.1,"evidence_tier":"studied"},{"concept_id":"urolithiasis","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":1.8,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"uterine_disorders","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":0.38,"evidence_tier":"sparse"}],"lead_score":null},"texts":{"cul:168-juniper-bush":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Juniper Bush","headword":"Juniper Bush","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"This admirable solar shrub is scarce to be paralleled for its virtues. The berries are hot in the third degree, and dry but in the first, being a most admirable counter-poison, and as great a resister of the pestilence, as any growing; they are excellent good against the biting of venomous beasts, they provoke urine exceedingly, and therefore are very available to dysuries and stranguaries. It is so powerful a remedy against the dropsy, that the very lye made of the ashes of the herb being drank, cures the disease. It provokes the terms, helps the fits of the mother, strengthens the stomach exceedingly, and expels the wind. Indeed there is scarce a better remedy for wind in any part of the body, or the cholic, than the chymical oil drawn from the berries; such country people as know not how to draw the chymical oil, may content themselves by eating ten or a dozen of the ripe berries every morning fasting. They are admirably good for a cough, shortness of breath, and consumption, pains in the belly, ruptures, cramps, and convulsions. They give safe and speedy delivery to women with child, they strengthen the brain exceedingly, help the memory, and fortify the sight by strengthening the optic nerves; are excellently good in all sorts of agues; help the gout and sciatica, and strengthen the limbs of the body. The ashes of the wood is a speedy remedy to such as have the scurvy, to rub their gums with. The berries stay all fluxes, help the hæmorrhoids or piles, and kill worms in children. A lye made of the ashes of the wood, and the body bathed with it, cures the itch, scabs and leprosy. The berries break the stone, procure appetite when it is lost, and are excellently good for all palsies, and falling-sickness.","spans":[{"start":161,"end":175,"concept_id":"poisoning","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":208,"end":218,"concept_id":"plague","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":272,"end":281,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":282,"end":290,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":304,"end":317,"concept_id":"diuresis","polarity":"action"},{"start":367,"end":375,"concept_id":"dysuria","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":380,"end":392,"concept_id":"dysuria","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":433,"end":439,"concept_id":"edema_dropsy","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":524,"end":542,"concept_id":"amenorrhea","polarity":"action"},{"start":562,"end":572,"concept_id":"uterine_disorders","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":574,"end":597,"concept_id":"dyspepsia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":615,"end":630,"concept_id":"flatulence","polarity":"action"},{"start":675,"end":703,"concept_id":"flatulence","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":712,"end":718,"concept_id":"colic","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":949,"end":954,"concept_id":"cough","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":956,"end":975,"concept_id":"asthma_dyspnea","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":981,"end":992,"concept_id":"tuberculosis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":994,"end":1012,"concept_id":"colic","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1024,"end":1030,"concept_id":"convulsions","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1036,"end":1047,"concept_id":"convulsions","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1059,"end":1083,"concept_id":"labor","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1153,"end":1159,"concept_id":"memory","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1165,"end":1182,"concept_id":"eye_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1255,"end":1260,"concept_id":"fever","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":